Hello Hackers,

Hmm. Apropos the ANSI driver:

There is a *small* bug in the TERMCAP library that comes with NetHack.
It seems that you have to put your ANSI screen driver *on the same
disk* as NetHack. The TERMCAP lib will not accept a TERMCAP
environment that starts with a drive prefix, e.g

TERMCAP=c:\etc\termcap (*invalid*)
TERMCAP=\etc\termcap   (*will do*)

The bug is easily fixed in "tgetent.c" (I think) where the TERMCAP
variable is examined.

